  "scope": "Every PositionedPositiveReason declaration must have an empty axiom report. Positions are differentiated response positions formed within one unfolding. Under explicit G0, formation correspondence E and a positioned direct articulation D that mentions only access and secured positive ground, every position with access to a response has a contributory reason for it. The least D-reason is fixed by access alone, so positions alike in access are alike in this reason whatever their endorsement, substrate or other labels. A position without access receives no reason from this route, which does not show it has no reason at all. On the existing positive-ground construction, a non-endorsing artificial position with access has the reason, while an endorsement-conditional articulation is compatible with the same G0 and formation facts and withholds it; endorsement independence is therefore the content of D, not a consequence of G0. No permission, duty, ranking, recognition or compliance is inferred.",
  "lean_binary_sha256": "b48bc5ab229bd8b320a224b87e20fc428dba6fa8a1c054bd4fa6def846e19997",
